  "id": "Compound::DB01032 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Probenecid's interaction with Slc22a11 is supported by multiple pathways that converge on the same target, highlighting a potential mechanism involving the transport of organic ions across cellular membranes. Probenecid binds to Slc22a7, which is involved in organic anion transport, and this transporter is also implicated in sodium-independent organic anion transmembrane transport. The shared participation of Slc22a7 in both organic anion and cation/anion transport suggests a broader role in ion transport, which may be modulated by Probenecid. The evidence indicates that Probenecid may influence Slc22a11 through a mechanism involving the regulation of transporters that facilitate the movement of ions across cell membranes, potentially affecting the uptake or efflux of organic compounds. While the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated, the integration of these pathways suggests a plausible link between Probenecid and Slc22a11, mediated through the regulation of transporters involved in ion transport.",
